# ── #1896: arm 2 also admits the review reflex's SKIP class (`automerge`) on a no-approval repo ──
# The mechanical -iac classes are CI-only BY DESIGN, so the reflex never reviews them and the
# bot-approval arm can never reach them; the label arm is what stops them stranding. The first row
# is the PIN (REDs on the pre-#1896 source); the rest are the negative controls that keep the label
# load-bearing (an ordinary unreviewed PR is still held; the label cannot bypass an approval-required
# repo's gate; and — PR#2303 review — the label alone is not enough: an `automerge` PR at
# CHANGES_REQUESTED is held, because the arm tests `reviewDecision == ""` AND the label).
automerge-no-approval-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-automerge-no-approval.jq | | picks | n=160 oid=auto160oid789
non-automerge-unreviewed-no-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-non-automerge-unreviewed.jq | | noop |
automerge-approval-required-no-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-automerge-approval-required.jq | | noop |
automerge-changes-requested-no-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-automerge-changes-requested.jq | | unstrand-no | n=163
# ── ADR-141 (minted in homelab PR#2003 — GitHub Actions majors merge on their own; this carve-out is one of its consequences): Renovate owns the currency of its UNTOUCHED GROUPED-ACTIONS branches (the two rules with
# rebaseWhen behind-base-branch); any other Renovate class still rides this updater (PR#2004 review) ─
renovate-untouched-no-update   | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq  |     | renovate-skip-probe1 | p1=150 oid=ren150oid789
renovate-worker-pushed-update  | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq  |     | picks-probe1-renovate | p1=150 n=150 oid=ren150oid789
renovate-untouched-cr-no-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-cr-behind.jq |     | unstrand-renovate-skip | n=151
renovate-other-class-no-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-other-class.jq |     | renovate-skip-probe1 | p1=152 oid=ren152oid789
# ── ADR-153 (2026-10-12): behind-base-branch is the ORG default, the skip covers EVERY Renovate branch
# (the `-other-class` row above flipped: on the pre-ADR-153 source it was updated, red on base) — and
# the ONE exception: untouched + merge-ready (armed, APPROVED, GREEN rollup) is updated, the fast path.
# Both rows below share add-renovate-approved; the axis is the row's pr-view-150 rollup.
renovate-untouched-green-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq |     | picks-probe1-renovate | p1=150 n=150 oid=ren150oid789
renovate-untouched-red-no-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq |    | renovate-skip-probe1 | p1=150 oid=ren150oid789
# Login shape (homelab#2007): the rows carry the REAL `app/homelab-renovate-1234` list shape — the raw-prefix
# test missed it and the updater edited a live grouped-Actions branch; `renovate-untouched-cr-no-update`
# keeps the plain `homelab-renovate-1234[bot]` shape so both spellings stay pinned.
# ── The hand-back (2026-10-24): the merge-ready exception's update MISSED (master moved again / the
# update pulled a red in), so the branch now carries the updater's MERGE commit — Renovate's edited-PR
# rule has disowned it, while `renovate_untouched` still reads untouched. Not merge-ready → tick
# Renovate's rebase box (its next run rebuilds the branch, the PR is Renovate's again). RED on the
# pre-hand-back source, which printed the "Renovate's to rebase" skip and left the zombie
# (homelab#2754, sleep-tracking#203 — 2026-10-20). `-ticked-noop` is the idempotence pin; `-cr-` is
# leg 2's twin. `renovate-superseded-cancel-green-update` is #2754's rollup: a CANCELLED duplicate `ci`
# beside its SUCCESS sibling is green (RED on the old `renovate_green`, which counted the CANCELLED).
renovate-updater-merged-red-handback   | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq |  | renovate-handback-probe1 | p1=150 oid=ren150oid789
renovate-updater-merged-ticked-noop    | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq |  | renovate-handback-ticked-probe1 | p1=150 oid=ren150oid789
renovate-updater-merged-cr-handback    | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-cr-behind.jq |  | unstrand-renovate-handback | n=151
renovate-superseded-cancel-green-update | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq |  | picks-probe1-renovate | p1=150 n=150 oid=ren150oid789
# ── 2026-10-24: the checks half of the probe is REST (commits/<sha>/check-runs + /status — the App's
# checks+statuses read; `--json statusCheckRollup` also selects checkSuite.workflowRun = actions:read,
# which homelab-merge lacks, so every PRIVATE-repo probe failed whole for 10+ days). A refused checks
# read HOLDS (rule #6) — never "not green", never a hand-back on a half-read.
renovate-checks-unreadable-hold | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-approved.jq | STUB_GH_api_repos_teststuffstash_testrepo_commits_ren150oid789_check_runs_per_page_100=fail | renovate-probe-hold | p1=150 oid=ren150oid789
# ── homelab#1985 residual 5 (2026-10-31): the hand-back sweep, leg 1b. The hand-back lived only INSIDE
# legs 1/2, so a merged-into Renovate PR outside their domains (current-but-red; a red codeowner park,
# which leg 1's pre-filter drops) was never probed and waited, disowned, until master moved under it.
# Leg 1b runs the same predicate over the complement. All four rows are RED on the pre-1b source (it
# never probed these PRs); the `-handback` rows are the pin, the `-noop` rows the negative controls,
# each RED under its own mutation (drop `renovate_merged_into` → untouched-current-red acts; drop the
# not-green test → merged-current-green acts): green + awaiting review is the reviewer's, an
# unmerged untouched branch is Renovate's own, and a sweep that acts on nothing prints nothing.
renovate-merged-current-red-handback | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-current-review.jq | | sweep-handback-probe1 | p1=153 oid=ren153oid789
renovate-merged-current-green-noop   | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-current-review.jq | | sweep-silent-probe1   | p1=153 oid=ren153oid789
renovate-untouched-current-red-noop  | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-current-review.jq | | sweep-silent-probe1   | p1=153 oid=ren153oid789
renovate-merged-park-red-handback    | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-park-red.jq       | | sweep-handback-probe1 | p1=154 oid=ren154oid789
# #3058 review: the sweep hands back only a CONCLUDED red (`renovate_red`). A current merged-into PR is
# most often the one leg 1 JUST updated, CI re-running — in-flight (`in_progress`) or not-yet-reported
# (zero checks) is silent; a hand-back there would discard the update. Both RED on the first-cut 1b
# source (which tested `! renovate_green`).
renovate-merged-current-pending-noop  | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-current-review.jq | | sweep-silent-probe1 | p1=153 oid=ren153oid789
renovate-merged-current-nochecks-noop | board | gh/pr-list.json @ patches/add-renovate-current-review.jq | | sweep-silent-probe1 | p1=153 oid=ren153oid789
